git-muse technical plan

Goal
- Build `git-muse`, exposed as `git muse`, to generate commit messages from staged Git changes.
- Default flow: read staged diff, generate candidate, let user confirm or edit, commit with `git commit -F <message-file>`.
- Keep Git behavior native: hooks, signing, editor, config, and credentials stay owned by system Git.

MVP commands
- `git muse`: interactive generate, confirm/edit, then commit.
- `git muse generate`: print generated message only.
- `git muse inspect`: show exact collected context before any LLM call.
- `git muse doctor`: check repo, staged changes, provider, model, and API key.

Non-goals for MVP
- No hook install.
- No automatic `git add`.
- No automatic `git reset` or split commit execution.
- No YAML config.
- No GUI/editor plugin.
- No new dependency until stdlib becomes painful.

Architecture
- `cmd`: CLI command routing.
- `internal/git`: thin wrapper around `os/exec` calling system `git`.
- `internal/diffctx`: staged diff/stat/status/branch/recent commits collection.
- `internal/commitmsg`: candidate model and Conventional Commit rendering.
- Future `internal/llm`: provider interface and OpenAI-compatible/Ollama clients.
- Future `internal/ui`: prompt and editor flows.

Git commands
- `git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree`
- `git diff --cached --stat`
- `git diff --cached --no-ext-diff --unified=3`
- `git status --porcelain=v1`
- `git log -5 --pretty=format:%s`
- `git branch --show-current`
- `git commit -F <message-file>`

Config
- Use Git config first.
- Read local before global.
- Add env overrides where useful.
- API keys only from environment variables.
- Do not store API keys with `git muse config set`.

Initial config keys
- `muse.provider`
- `muse.model`
- `muse.baseUrl`
- `muse.format`
- `muse.language`
- `muse.count`
- `muse.maxDiffBytes`
- `muse.temperature`

Provider plan
- Start with `compatible` provider for OpenAI-compatible APIs.
- Add `ollama` provider for local models.
- Provider interface: `Generate(ctx, req)`, `Validate(ctx)`, `Name()`.
- Model returns strict JSON candidates; app renders final commit text.

Candidate JSON
- `type`: Conventional Commit type.
- `scope`: optional scope.
- `subject`: required, <= 72 chars.
- `body`: optional lines.
- `confidence`: optional score.
- `warnings`: optional model warnings.

Safety
- Only staged diff by default.
- Never build shell strings for commit.
- Use process args and `git commit -F`.
- Show real payload through `git muse inspect`.
- Redact or exclude obvious secrets before LLM calls.
- Delete temp message file after commit attempt.

Diff filtering plan
- Exclude `.env`, `.env.*`, `*.pem`, `*.key`, `*.crt`, `*.p12`.
- Exclude generated/vendor paths: `dist/**`, `build/**`, `vendor/**`, `node_modules/**`.
- Truncate huge diff by `muse.maxDiffBytes`.
- Later: summarize lockfiles instead of sending full lockfile diffs.

Milestones
- M1: compileable CLI skeleton with `generate`, `inspect`, `doctor`.
- M2: config reader and effective config output.
- M3: OpenAI-compatible provider, strict JSON parsing, one retry on invalid JSON.
- M4: Ollama provider.
- M5: interactive confirm/edit/regenerate and `git commit -F`.
- M6: filtering, redaction, truncation, and inspect details.
- M7: release binaries and install docs.

Checks
- `go test ./...`
- `go run . help`
- `go run . doctor` inside repo with staged changes.
